  "conclusions": [
    "A high diagnostic floor removes the low-Rs regime in which the prior W04 floor-off run had explicit-step runaway; corrected analysis of floor-off gives Kmax=28200.05, with 119448 non-finite channel samples and 51734 sign crossings. This protection is conditional on the conductance bound used by the C++ floor.",
    "In BR25 the Rs/Rm>=1 floor did not bind; it converged and the evaluator reported 8/8, target detected, zero false alarms. The matrix harness marked this diagnostic row tipr_mismatch because the expected canonical TipR profile was intentionally not the diagnostic outcome.",
    "In BR480, Rs/Rm>=1 kept corrected Kmax at 0.15313 with no sign/envelope violations, but C++ still refused on invalid_peak_no_recovery. Peak threshold 1e-8 also did not rescue BR480; that run has corrected Kmax=0.64948 and the final target peak remained about 1.095e-9.",
    "In the Rs/Rm=0.1 ablation, corrected Kmax=3.6125; a fixed-sign input and the exact C++ update reproduce the observed channel sign flips and overshoot. This is direct evidence of explicit-Euler instability in that tested condition.",
    "A membrane aggregate can be negative while its individual signed channels preserve Type; the BR25 aggregate minimum does not imply a channel crossing."
  ],
  "diagnostic_method_correction": {
    "issue": "The previous analyzer read SumSynapticInput state as conductance. In the serialized trainer snapshot this state can remain zero while the SynapticInputs vector used by NPulseChannel::ACalculate2 is nonzero.",
    "fix": "Parse and sum SynapticInputs from the C++ snapshot; retain SumSynapticInput only as a fallback for older telemetry without the vector.",
    "impact": "The prior explicit-step K estimates in this artifact were understated and are replaced by the corrected values above. Channel outputs, sign/envelope counts, training outcomes, and quality metrics are unchanged.",
    "regression_test": "test_step_gain_uses_synaptic_input_vector_when_sum_state_is_stale; test_high_synaptic_conductance_reports_unstable_explicit_step"
  },
